<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP steel workers vote against strike.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP steel workers vote against strike.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd said a meeting of workers at its Newcastle steelworks on Wednesday morning had decided against taking strike action.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a meeting this morning of employees and they decided there would be no strike,&quot; a spokesman for the company's Newcastle operations, north of Sydney, told Reuters.</p>
<p>BHP chairman Brian Loton told the company's annual meeting on Tuesday it did not plan to close its Newcastle plant but was studying all options and opportunities for the integrated steelworks. A number of city newspapers on Wednesday suggested a closure might eventually be considered. -- Sydney 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
